        "question": {
          ":question/id": "73ed6174-345b-539d-a3f9-902aeddd98fe",
          ":question/problem": "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 y \\right)} + 2$ on $2 x - 3 y>0$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant. The additive constant has zero partial derivatives.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y)&=\\frac{1}{2 x - 3 y}\\cdot\\left(2\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3 y} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y)&=\\frac{1}{2 x - 3 y}\\cdot\\left(-3\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{3}{2 x - 3 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y)&=\\left(\\frac{2}{2 x - 3 y}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(- \\frac{3}{2 x - 3 y}\\right)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
