        "question": {
          ":question/id": "c7806450-9a47-5be1-90e6-9e3da6917ba1",
          ":question/problem": "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=z e^{2 x z + y}$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant. In the $z$ derivative, both the coordinate prefactor and the argument depend on $z$, so use both the product rule and the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=z\\cdot e^{2 x z + y}\\cdot\\left(2 z\\right) \\\\ &=2 z^{2} e^{2 x z + y} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=z\\cdot e^{2 x z + y}\\cdot\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &=z e^{2 x z + y} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=e^{2 x z + y}+z\\cdot e^{2 x z + y}\\cdot\\left(2 x\\right) \\\\ &=2 x z e^{2 x z + y} + e^{2 x z + y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(2 z^{2} e^{2 x z + y}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(z e^{2 x z + y}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(2 x z e^{2 x z + y} + e^{2 x z + y}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
